{
  "protocol_name": "Serial 1:10 dilution of culture in sterile saline",
  "description": "Makes six 10-fold serial dilutions (10^-1 to 10^-6) of an optimum-growth culture in 0.9% sterile saline across one 96-well plate column set, so one of the dilutions should yield 10-100 CFU/mL when plated off-deck.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Kept the 1:10 dilution ratio from the text: each step is 10 uL transferred into 90 uL saline (total 100 uL). The parenthetical '1 mL in 10 mL' would be 1:11, so I followed the stated 1:10 ratio and scaled volumes to the plate (uL instead of mL).",
    "Number of dilutions was not specified; chose 6 (10^-1 to 10^-6), columns 1-6, to cover the 10-100 CFU/mL target. Adjust if the expected count is different.",
    "Dilution 1 (column 1) is culture plus saline at 1:10; column k holds the 10^-k dilution.",
    "Diluent is pre-loaded using 270 uL aspirations dispensed as 3 x 90 uL, to save tip columns on the rack.",
    "Each transfer is preceded by mixing the source well (50 uL aspirate and dispense back) before 10 uL is removed, per the rule that the well must be mixed before liquid is taken from it.",
    "Culture is in a reservoir, not a tube, so all 8 channels can aspirate it in parallel.",
    "Tips: 300 uL filter, the smallest tip that holds the 270 uL diluent aspiration. Tip columns 1-9 are used once each.",
    "Plate: 96-well 289.7 uL Cos_96_PCR already on deck; wells hold at most 100 uL, well below capacity.",
    "Reservoir volumes are assumed. Diluent: 1000 uL loaded (540 uL needed plus dead volume). Culture: 200 uL loaded (only 10 uL is needed; reservoir sized for margin).",
    "Plating on agar, colony counting and incubation are not robot tasks and are not in the steps; the user must plate the chosen dilution and count colonies after incubation."
  ],
